  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37144010",
      "title": "Adding a Side Drawer",
      "lectureOrder": 171,
      "videoOrder": 159,
      "sourceHash": "aac8f8fe6fd5045f3490adea3d6842f82275e029690542c0a06521ed46799a55",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "So, now that we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "our tab based navigation working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "and we can mark items as favorites",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "and see them under the Favorites tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "it's time to add this side drawer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "which I mentioned earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 18.21,
          "en": "A side drawer which we can open up to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "to a filters screen on which we can set various filters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "which will then impact which meals we see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.443,
          "en": "when we select a category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "And just like tabs, which we added with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 36.09,
          "en": "of bottomNavigationBar on Scaffold,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "such a side drawer is an absolutely common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "and standard feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "and therefore very easy to add with Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "Indeed, it's again the Scaffold widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "that allows us to add a drawer to this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "because that's also important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "Side drawers are added on a per screen basis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "If you want to have a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 62.01,
          "en": "that opens the side drawer on a specific screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "in the app bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 67.053,
          "en": "you have to add it to the Scaffold of that screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.89,
          "end": 71.03999999999999,
          "en": "So, here, if I want to have a side drawer on both tabs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.03999999999999,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "I have to add the side drawer to the tabs screen scaffold,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 77.193,
          "en": "and that's exactly where I'm at in my code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "So, there on Scaffold, we can then add the drawer parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 83.91,
          "en": "And as you can already see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "you also got a couple of other drawer related parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 90.53999999999999,
          "en": "that allow you to basically configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "the behavior of the drawer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 96.12,
          "en": "and listen to certain events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.12,
          "end": 99.50999999999999,
          "en": "But here, I'll simply add the drawer parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "and this wants a widget in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "a widget that will be presented as the drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "Now, for that Flutter has the built-in Drawer widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "which is simply a widget that's optimized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "for being shown as a side drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 120.6,
          "en": "But since I'm about to add a lot of content to that drawer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 122.91,
          "en": "I'll actually create a brand new widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.91,
          "end": 126.12,
          "en": "my own custom widget, in the widgets folder therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.12,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "because this will now not act as a screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.623,
          "en": "but as the side drawer instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 135.36,
          "en": "And I'll name it main_drawer.dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.36,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "Of course, as always, all these names are up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 141.243,
          "en": "But in this file, I'll then add a new class, MainDrawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "And this class will extend StatelessWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "because even though this drawer will then provide buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "that take us to different screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "we'll again perform this navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "with help of the Navigator object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "and not by setting some state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "hence the Drawer widget can be stateless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "Now, in this drawer class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 166.92000000000002,
          "en": "we therefore as always add the build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 169.413,
          "en": "and also a const MainDrawer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.25,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "where at the moment I only accept and forward the key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 175.263,
          "en": "as we always do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.19,
          "end": 177.99,
          "en": "And now here in the build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 180.573,
          "en": "I will return that built-in Drawer widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 183.15,
          "en": "Now this Drawer widget gives you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "a bunch of configurational options, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 188.88,
          "en": "setting the background color of the drawer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 191.25,
          "en": "or the color of the background shadow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 193.41,
          "en": "that will be displayed below the drawer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.41,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "or with elevation, you can basically define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 199.443,
          "en": "how much drop shadow you want to have behind the drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.31,
          "end": 204.18,
          "en": "But here I'll simply set the child which defines the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.18,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "inside of the drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "And as I mentioned, the Drawer, which it is already a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "that's optimized to be presented as a drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 214.95,
          "en": "So, it will for example, automatically make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.95,
          "end": 219.24,
          "en": "that it takes the entire screen height and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.24,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "So, here, as a child, I'll then add a column",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 223.68,
          "en": "because I wanna have multiple items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.68,
          "end": 226.023,
          "en": "above each other in that drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.89,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "And for that of course we set our children here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 232.14,
          "en": "in this column as we always do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.14,
          "end": 235.35,
          "en": "And then the different children that I do wanna set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 238.47,
          "en": "are basically a header at the top of the drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.47,
          "end": 242.7,
          "en": "And then below that, a couple of clickable or tappable items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 244.683,
          "en": "that take us to different screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 247.11,
          "en": "Now for the header we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.11,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "the built-in DrawerHeader widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.14,
          "en": "which is another widget optimized for its role,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.14,
          "end": 256.95,
          "en": "in this case, optimized for being used inside of a drawer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.95,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "to show them header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "as you might guess, at the top of the drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 264.48,
          "en": "Now, DrawerHeader can be configured in different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.48,
          "end": 267.3,
          "en": "and accepts different parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 270.99,
          "en": "And I will for example also soon add a decoration to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.99,
          "end": 274.35,
          "en": "to style it basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 278.07,
          "en": "And also add some padding, which is supported here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.07,
          "end": 279.87,
          "en": "with the padding parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.87,
          "end": 280.98,
          "en": "And I'll start with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 280.98,
          "end": 285.273,
          "en": "and give it a padding of 20 in all directions like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.44,
          "end": 290.43,
          "en": "And then in addition to this, I'll also re-add decoration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.43,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "and set this to a BoxDecoration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 295.38,
          "en": "as we did many times before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.38,
          "end": 298.32,
          "en": "for other widgets as well in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.32,
          "end": 301.8,
          "en": "And I'm doing this so that I can add a gradient here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.8,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "And I guess that was the most common scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "where I used BoxDecoration thus far in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 309.39,
          "en": "for adding gradients to widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 309.39,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "And I'm doing the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "Now, the gradient is created as we always do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 318.87,
          "en": "with the LinearGradient class here, provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 318.87,
          "end": 323.87,
          "en": "And then we can set our colors and then also begin and end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.21,
          "end": 328.5,
          "en": "Now, for the colors, I'll use some colors from my theme",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.5,
          "end": 333.15,
          "en": "with Theme.of(context) using this context object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 333.15,
          "end": 336.3,
          "en": "which we get automatically in the build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336.3,
          "end": 339.12,
          "en": "And then here I'll reach out to my colorScheme",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.12,
          "end": 343.05,
          "en": "and use the primaryContainer as a starting color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 343.05,
          "end": 346.68,
          "en": "And for the end color, I'll also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 346.68,
          "end": 348.75,
          "en": "colorScheme.primaryContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.75,
          "end": 350.43,
          "en": "So I'll copy that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.43,
          "end": 353.4,
          "en": "but then I'll add some opacity to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.4,
          "end": 356.85,
          "en": "to have a slight gradient between the same colors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.85,
          "end": 359.733,
          "en": "but where one color has some transparency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.75,
          "end": 362.82,
          "en": "And then I'll begin with that gradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.82,
          "end": 367.56,
          "en": "in the top left corner with Alignment.topLeft,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 367.56,
          "end": 371.793,
          "en": "and I'll end in the bottom right corner like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 373.17,
          "end": 377.22,
          "en": "And with that I got some styling added to the DrawerHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 377.22,
          "end": 379.14,
          "en": "Of course, it also needs a child though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.14,
          "end": 382.8,
          "en": "which simply defines the main content inside of this header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.8,
          "end": 386.64,
          "en": "And for that here, I'll add a row as a child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 386.64,
          "end": 389.43,
          "en": "because I wanna have multiple items next to each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 389.43,
          "end": 391.59,
          "en": "inside of that DrawerHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 391.59,
          "end": 395.04,
          "en": "And the items I do want to have next to each other here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 395.04,
          "end": 400.04,
          "en": "are an Icon and then a SizedBox to add some spacing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 400.23,
          "end": 401.823,
          "en": "and then some Text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 402.87,
          "end": 407.49,
          "en": "Now, for the spacing, I'll use a width of 18 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.49,
